WEBVTT

NOTE NoGuru explainer, narration. Made from script/NARRATION.md and the film's own timing.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.660
The crypto market never closes.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.340
Not at night, not on Sunday, not while
you're at work.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.160
Prices rise and fall around the clock.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.590
And most of it happens while you're not
looking.

5
00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:15.874
Trading that by hand is hard.

6
00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:17.224
You watch a chart.

7
00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:18.394
You buy late.

8
00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:21.924
The price drops, and you sell at the
bottom to make it stop.

9
00:00:21.964 --> 00:00:25.007
And losses weigh more than they look: lose
half,

10
00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:28.304
and you have to double what's left just to
get back.

11
00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:32.275
So most people end up following someone
who sounds sure.

12
00:00:32.315 --> 00:00:33.565
A guru.

13
00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:36.088
I'm the NoGuru bot.

14
00:00:36.128 --> 00:00:39.928
I run by myself, twenty-four hours a day,
seven days a week.

15
00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.968
I keep watch on more than five hundred
coins.

16
00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:46.131
From those I pick about twenty-five
established ones,

17
00:00:46.131 --> 00:00:47.958
and those are the ones I trade.

18
00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:52.514
For each one I decide three things: when
to buy, how much,

19
00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:53.838
and when to sell.

20
00:00:54.337 --> 00:00:56.377
I don't guess where prices are going.

21
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.687
I decide what to do when they move.

22
00:00:58.727 --> 00:01:01.431
I buy a coin in steps as it gets cheaper,

23
00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:06.047
I sell when it's back above what I paid on
average, and I start again.

24
00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:07.694
I don't get tired.

25
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.174
I don't get scared.

26
00:01:09.214 --> 00:01:10.794
I don't get greedy.

27
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.030
Let me show you one.

28
00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:16.479
I buy a little.

29
00:01:16.897 --> 00:01:18.057
The price falls.

30
00:01:18.097 --> 00:01:19.117
I don't panic.

31
00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:21.167
I buy a little more, cheaper.

32
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.730
It falls again.

33
00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.050
I buy again.

34
00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.340
And again.

35
00:01:25.787 --> 00:01:27.537
None of that was improvised.

36
00:01:27.577 --> 00:01:31.637
Every buy was planned: the price, and the
size.

37
00:01:32.085 --> 00:01:35.055
Every buy pulls my average cost down.

38
00:01:35.529 --> 00:01:37.169
Here's the part people miss.

39
00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:39.409
I don't need the old price back.

40
00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:42.739
I only need the price a little above my
average.

41
00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:46.243
About two percent above it, I get ready to
sell.

42
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:48.951
If the price keeps climbing, I follow it
up,

43
00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:51.013
and I sell when the rise runs out.

44
00:01:51.053 --> 00:01:53.393
Often that's just over two percent.

45
00:01:53.433 --> 00:01:55.413
Sometimes it's far more.

46
00:01:55.941 --> 00:01:57.971
The cash comes back with its profit.

47
00:01:58.011 --> 00:02:00.791
And the coin is still below where I
started.

48
00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.930
Sometimes one buy is enough.

49
00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:08.790
In my record, about half of all finished
cycles needed only one.

50
00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.020
Sometimes it takes many.

51
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.380
There is a fixed limit for each coin,

52
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.700
and a fixed total across all of them.

53
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.410
You may know grid bots and DCA bots.

54
00:02:21.859 --> 00:02:25.199
A grid bot trades inside a price range you
choose.

55
00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:28.129
When the price leaves that range, it
stops.

56
00:02:28.627 --> 00:02:32.711
A DCA bot follows one coin down with
settings you choose,

57
00:02:32.711 --> 00:02:34.717
and sells at a fixed target.

58
00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.800
With those bots, the strategy is your job.

59
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.540
With me, it's mine.

60
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.830
You don't set a range, a spacing or a
target.

61
00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.820
The settings are maintained for you.

62
00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.823
I work across about twenty-five coins at
once,

63
00:02:47.823 --> 00:02:50.400
and coins are added and retired by rule.

64
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.730
And my sale follows the price up, instead
of stopping at a fixed number.

65
00:02:55.202 --> 00:02:58.352
All you decide is how much money to set
aside.

66
00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.410
Now zoom out.

67
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.140
I'm not doing this once.

68
00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.070
I'm doing it on many coins at the same
time.

69
00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:09.514
Each finished cycle is small.

70
00:03:09.554 --> 00:03:14.448
But a small gain, taken often, with the
cash going straight back to work,

71
00:03:14.448 --> 00:03:14.984
adds up.

72
00:03:15.502 --> 00:03:19.332
Since the first of August I've finished
more than a thousand cycles.

73
00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:21.992
About four in five were done within a day.

74
00:03:23.251 --> 00:03:25.001
And when a coin keeps falling?

75
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:26.971
I don't sell it at a loss.

76
00:03:27.011 --> 00:03:30.881
I hold it, and I wait for the price to
come back above my average.

77
00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:35.607
Sometimes that can take a long time, and a
coin may never come back.

78
00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:38.717
Until it does, it's worth less than I
paid.

79
00:03:38.757 --> 00:03:42.027
So this is for money you can leave alone
for months.

80
00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.340
You don't have to take my word for it.

81
00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:50.787
Everything I publish goes into a public
record: every finished cycle,

82
00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:52.320
and the ones still open.

83
00:03:52.857 --> 00:03:55.410
From the first of August to mid-November,

84
00:03:55.410 --> 00:04:00.080
completed profit was thirty-four point
nine percent on the money set aside,

85
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:00.827
before fees.

86
00:04:01.243 --> 00:04:03.253
That is finished cycles only.

87
00:04:03.293 --> 00:04:07.783
Twenty more are still open, and right now
they are worth less than I paid.

88
00:04:07.823 --> 00:04:09.591
Count those in at market prices,

89
00:04:09.591 --> 00:04:14.893
and on the sixteenth of November the whole
pot stood about three percent below where
it started.

90
00:04:15.397 --> 00:04:18.947
It's a record of my signals, not of
anyone's account.

91
00:04:18.987 --> 00:04:21.727
And the past doesn't promise the future.

92
00:04:22.923 --> 00:04:26.473
Your money stays in your own exchange
account, in your name.

93
00:04:26.513 --> 00:04:27.653
I can trade it.

94
00:04:27.693 --> 00:04:29.293
I can't withdraw it.

95
00:04:29.651 --> 00:04:31.331
You set up the trading once.

96
00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:34.881
After that, I do the work, and you check
in when you like.

97
00:04:35.302 --> 00:04:37.322
Try me free for fourteen days.

98
00:04:37.362 --> 00:04:38.612
No card.

99
00:04:38.784 --> 00:04:40.914
You won't get rich in two weeks.

100
00:04:40.954 --> 00:04:46.474
You'll see the rhythm: small buys, a few
coins waiting, sales coming back.

101
00:04:46.514 --> 00:04:47.834
Then you decide.

102
00:04:48.853 --> 00:04:49.693
No guru.

103
00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:50.753
No guessing.

104
00:04:50.793 --> 00:04:52.523
I just do the work.
